-- title:
--   Cotangent length bound: ordinary versus flat at p
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation domain that is complete for its maximal-adic topology, let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal O$ (a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite level), let $p$ be an odd prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$. Let $D_0$ be deformation-ring data for $\bar\rho$ with the condition [`GaloisRep.flatCondition`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47) at $(p,S)$ — determinant cyclotomic in the sense of `DetIsCyclotomic p`, the predicate `IsFlatAt p`, and `IsUnramifiedAt q` for every prime $q \notin S$ — and $D'$ deformation-ring data for [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28) at the same $(p,S)$, where `IsFlatAt p` is replaced by `IsOrdinaryAt p`; each consists of a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with residue field generated by that of $\mathcal O$, an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$, a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ over $R$ of the given type whose residual representation is equivalent to $\bar\rho$ over the residue field of $R$, universal among such deformations. Let $\theta : D'.R \to D_0.R$ and $x_0 : D_0.R \to \mathcal O$ be local $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, with $\theta$ surjective and the base change of $D'.\rho$ along $\theta$ equivalent to $D_0.\rho$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $P$, and write $V$ for the representation space of the base change of $D_0.\rho$ along $x_0$. Let $L \subseteq V$ be an $\mathcal O$-submodule spanned by the first member of some basis of $V$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, such that every element of the image of the inertia subgroup acts trivially on $V/L$, and let $\alpha \in \mathcal O$ be such that every Frobenius element at $p$ in the decomposition subgroup (in the sense of `IsFrobeniusAt`) acts on $V/L$ by $\alpha$. Then, with $\mathfrak p' = \ker(x_0 \circ \theta)$ and $\mathfrak p_0 = \ker x_0$, the $\mathcal O$-lengths (in $\mathbb N_\infty$) satisfy $\ell_{\mathcal O}(\mathfrak p'/\mathfrak p'^2) \le \ell_{\mathcal O}(\mathfrak p_0/\mathfrak p_0^2) + \ell_{\mathcal O}(\mathcal O/(\alpha^2-1))$.
--
--   This is the Galois-side bound for the rung at $p$ comparing the ordinary and the flat (crystalline) deformation conditions: passing from the flat universal ring to the ordinary one increases the cotangent length at an $\mathcal O$-point by at most the length of $\mathcal O/(\alpha^2-1)$, the local invariant $c_p$ attached to the unit root $\alpha$ of Frobenius. It is used in the comparison of Hecke algebras and deformation rings for the ordinary condition at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_DeformationRingData_length_cotangent_le_add_of_ordinaryCondition_of_flatCondition.lean

